    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0277" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Chinese Executive Yuan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Soong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d137-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                        calendar="gregorian" type="received-date" when="1947-10-01">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide-Mémoire</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Informal Suggestion—Without Commitment</hi>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>I.</label>
                    <item>Five-men Committee to meet first to discuss Communist participation in
                        State Council.</item>
                    <label>II.</label>
                    <item>
                        <list>
                            <item>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) Following this first meeting a
                                3-men Committee to meet and decide the areas to which Communist
                                troops will be assigned.</item>
                            <item>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) Dates will be set for the
                                movement of Communist troops to, designated areas.</item>
                            <item>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) Truce teams will be sent to
                                observe the movement of these troops.</item>
                            <item>(<hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>) Upon the acceptance by the
                                Communist delegates of the areas where Communist troops will be
                                stationed and the dates set for their removal to those areas,
                                cease-fire order will forthwith be given.</item>
                            <item>(<hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>) When the Communist troops have
                                reached the areas assigned to them, they will be incorporated into
                                the National Army, and trained and equipped like other national
                                divisions.</item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d137-f1" n="33" type="source" xml:id="d137-f1-content">
                <p>Handed to Dr. Stuart on October 1.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
